+   ! A homogeneous strain can be differentiated using either of two
+   ! geometrical conventions for an LAPW partition.  In the usual analytic
+   ! derivation the muffin-tin is transported by the affine coordinate map.
+   ! A WIEN2k finite-difference calculation, however, normally keeps RMT
+   ! fixed in Bohr.  Reynolds' transport theorem then leaves a boundary
+   ! (shape-derivative) term
+   !
+   !   RMT^3 int dOmega n_alpha n_beta [L_I(RMT)-L_MT(RMT)] .
+   !
+   ! The potential and tangential-gradient pieces cancel when the augmented
+   ! wave function is continuous at the sphere.  In Rydberg units the
+   ! remaining kinetic candidate is therefore the jump in the squared radial
+   ! derivative.  A_surf2 is the interstitial radial derivative, while the
+   ! array below reconstructs the muffin-tin derivative including all local
+   ! orbitals.  We keep this contribution separate from buf_APW: the latter
+   ! is the familiar APW+lo derivative-discontinuity term and is not the
+   ! fixed-RMT shape derivative.
+   !
+   ! This is initially a guarded diagnostic.  l2main accumulates and
+   ! symmetrizes it, and symmetrization_stress applies it only when
+   ! WIEN_STRESS_RMT_SHAPE=GRAD is set explicitly.
+   allocate(dmt_surf((lmax2+1)*(lmax2+1),nume))
+   allocate(psi_surf((lmax2+1)*(lmax2+1),nume))
+   allocate(tmt_surf((lmax2+1)*(lmax2+1),nume))
+   dmt_surf = zeroc
+   psi_surf = zeroc
+   tmt_surf = zeroc
+
